alusian philosopher, physician and judge of the twelfth century who served the Almohad caliphs.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aveyron"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/aveyron.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Aveyron</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Aveyron is a department in southern France, in the Occitanie region, covering most of the former province of Rouergue.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/avgustyn-voloshyn"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/avgustyn-voloshyn.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Avgustyn Voloshyn</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Avgustyn Voloshyn was a Greek Catholic priest, teacher and Ukrainian political leader in Subcarpathian Ruthenia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/avicenna"><span class="enc-name">Avicenna</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Avicenna, Ibn Sina, was a Persian philosopher and physician born near Bukhara under the Samanids.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/avidius-cassius"><span class="enc-name">Avidius Cassius</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Gaius Avidius Cassius was a Roman general born in Syria.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/avienus"><span class="enc-name">Avienus</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Avienus (Rufius Festus Avienius) was a Latin poet of the 4th century CE who adapted Greek works on geography and astronomy into verse.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/avignon"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/avignon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Avignon</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span cla