><a href="/encyclopedia/ayrarat"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ayrarat.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ayrarat</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Ayrarat was a central province of historic Armenia, in the plain of the Aras river around Mount Ararat.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ayrshire"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ayrshire.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ayrshire</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Ayrshire is a historic county in south-west Scotland, on the Firth of Clyde, divided into the districts of Carrick, Kyle and Cunninghame.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ayub-khan"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ayub-khan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ayub Khan</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ayub Khan was a Pakistani general who became commander-in-chief in 1951 and seized power in the coup of October 1958, ruling as president until 1969.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ayudha-dynasty"><span class="enc-name">Ayudha dynasty</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Ayudha dynasty ruled Kannauj in the late eighth and early ninth centuries CE, when the city was the prize of the tripartite struggle between the Pratiharas, Palas…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ayuka-khan"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ayuka-khan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ayuka Khan</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ayuka Khan was ruler of the Kalmyks on the lower Volga from 1669 to 1724, the most powerful leader of the Kalmyk Khanate.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ayung-river"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ayung-river.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ayung River</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Ayung is the longest river on Bali, Indonesia, flowing south from the central highlands past Ubud to the sea near Sanur.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ayurbarwada-buyantu-khan"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ayurbarwada-buyantu-khan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ayurbarwada Buyantu Khan</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ayurbarwada Buyantu Khan, known by the temple name Renzong, was emperor of the Yuan dynasty from 1311 to 1320.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ayushiridara"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ayushiridara.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ayushiridara</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ayushiridara, known as Biligtü Khan, was the son of Toghon Temür, the last Yuan emperor of China, and ruled the Northern Yuan in Mongolia from 1370 to 1378.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ayutthaya-kingdom"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ayutthaya-kingdom.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ayutthaya Kingdom</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Ayutthaya Kingdom was a Siamese state founded in 1351 in central Thailand.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ayyanadikal-thiruvadikal"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ayyanadikal-thiruvadikal.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ayyanadikal Thiruvadikal</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ayyanadikal Thiruvadikal was the ruler of Venad in southern Kerala in the mid-ninth century, under the overlordship of the Chera Perumal king Sthanu Ravi.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ayyubid-empire"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ayyubid-empire.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ayyubid Empire</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Ayyubid Empire was a Sunni Muslim dynasty founded by Saladin, who ended the Fatimid Caliphate in Egypt in 1171 and united Egypt and Syria.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/az-zahir-ghazi"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/az-zahir-ghazi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Az-Zahir Ghazi</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Az-Zahir Ghazi was a son of Saladin and Ayyubid ruler of Aleppo from 1186 to 1216.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/azad-kashmir"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/azad-kashmir.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Azad Kashmir</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Azad Kashmir is a self-governing territory administered by Pakistan in the western part of the former princely state of Jammu and Kashmir, with its capital at…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/azad-khan-afghan"><span class="enc-name">Azad Khan Afghan</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Azad Khan Afghan was an Afghan commander who rose to power in north-western Iran after the death of Nader Shah.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/azai-hisamasa"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/azai-hisamasa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="en